# Lentil Sandwich

Based on [https://saucestache.com/why-you-should-be-eating-lentil-sandwich](https://saucestache.com/why-you-should-be-eating-lentil-sandwich) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250815093321/https://saucestache.com/why-you-should-be-eating-lentil-sandwich/))

{ rating="4" image="lentil_sandwich.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] [White Onion]{ ing="white-onion" }, diced
- [ ] [Green Pepper]{ ing="green-pepper" }, diced
- [ ] 1-2 [Carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, diced
- [ ] 2-3 [Garlic Cloves]{ ing="garlic-cloves" }, diced
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1 cup [Green or Red lentils]{ ing="green-or-red-lentils" } (or rice)
- [ ] 1.5 cups [Vegetable Broth]{ ing="vegetable-broth" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [Sauce]{ ing="sauce" } (Curry, Steak, etc.)
- [ ] [Bread]{ ing="bread" }

## Recipe

1. Prep the vegetables and garlic, then saute in a deep pan for a few minutes
1. Add [lentils]{ ing="green-or-red-lentils" }, [broth]{ ing="vegetable-broth" }, and [sauce]{ ing="sauce" }. Mix and let simmer for 20 min

## Notes

- If using a 2 cup can of broth, you can scale up the ingredients, as long as they fit in the pan, by adding another 1/4 cup of rice or lentils and extra vegetables. Or you can cook the extras separately if using a main sauce that is too flavorful for kids
- Green lentils hold shape better for sandwiches and have a peppery flavor; red lentils cook faster (15 min vs 20 min), break down into a creamy spreadable texture, and have a nutty flavor
- Optional: Add a squeeze of lemon or lime before serving
